  <h1>Should We Train Speculative Drafters On-Policy?</h1>
  <p class="lead">Drafters in speculative decoding are usually trained offline on teacher-forced data and bolted on as an attachment to the main model. But what if we trained the drafter like a distilled student — on its <i>own</i> self-generated drafts, the way we distill a big model into a small one? It turns out the frontier already answers this: <b>yes</b> — and the reason is subtle, because speculative decoding's lossless verifier means on-policy training buys pure <i>speed</i>, never quality.</p>
