          <div class="step-title">Step 0 — teacher-forced base (offline)</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Draft position 1 sees the target's true feature. This is plain EAGLE / SpecForge warm-up.</div>
          <div class="step-code">h₁ = target_feature ; loss += KD(draft(h₁), target_logits₁)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Step 1 — feed the drafter's own feature</div>
          <div class="step-desc">For position 2, swap in the feature the drafter just produced — not the target's. Attention mask is shifted to keep causality.</div>
          <div class="step-code">h₂ = draft_feature₁ ; loss += KD(draft(h₂), target_logits₂)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Step 2 — unroll again</div>
          <div class="step-desc">Position 3 conditions on the drafter's step-2 output. The drafter now sees the same compounding it will face at inference.</div>
          <div class="step-code">h₃ = draft_feature₂ ; loss += KD(draft(h₃), target_logits₃)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Step 3 — full harmonized window (HASS)</div>
          <div class="step-desc">After 3–4 unrolled steps the train/inference contexts match. Acceptance length jumps — no extra inference cost.</div>
          <div class="step-code">acc_len: 3.78 → 5.15 (LLaMA2-7B, EAGLE → HASS)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
